Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Compile the bucket allocator against one freestanding shim
Upstream: apr-util 1.6.3
Upstream-Archive: https://archive.apache.org/dist/apr/apr-util-1.6.3.tar.gz
Upstream-SHA256: 2b74d8932703826862ca305b094eef2983c27b39d5c9414442e9976a9acf1983
Build-Variants: native port, Capstone domain
Depends-On: none
Apply-From: upstream source root, with patch --batch --forward --fuzz=0 -p1

apr_buckets_alloc.c includes five apr-util and APR headers and <stdlib.h>, and
apr_buckets.h pulls ten more in behind them. Replace every one with
adapted/apr_bucket_shim.h, which carries the node geometry verbatim from
apr_buckets.h -- APR_BUCKET_ALLOC_SIZE is 2*sizeof(union apr_bucket_structs),
and a shim that invented that size would silently change the block layout --
and declares what the allocator asks for and nothing else. The allocator is
untouched: this patch removes four include lines and adds one.

This is the census seam (../build-buckets-census.sh) recorded as a patch, so
the prepared source is reproducible from the archive and the patch alone.

--- a/buckets/apr_buckets_alloc.c
+++ b/buckets/apr_buckets_alloc.c
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include "apr_bucket_shim.h"
 /* Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one or more
  * contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file distributed with
  * this work for additional information regarding copyright ownership.
@@ -14,11 +15,7 @@
  * limitations under the License.
  */
 
-#include <stdlib.h>
 
-#include "apr_buckets.h"
-#include "apr_allocator.h"
-#include "apr_version.h"
 
 #define ALLOC_AMT (8192 - APR_MEMNODE_T_SIZE)
 
@@ -209,7 +206,6 @@
 
 #ifdef APR_BUCKET_DEBUG
 #if APR_HAVE_STDLIB_H
-#include <stdlib.h>
 #endif
 static void check_not_already_free(node_header_t *node)
 {
